            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of the bicycle ergometry test on lipid peroxidation processes in patients with ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effect of bicycle ergometry on lipid peroxidation was examined in 43 coronary patients. An increase in malonic dialdehyde, a secondary product of lipid peroxidation, was detected in patients with post-infarction cardiosclerosis, an evidence of intensified lipid peroxidation in systemic tissues. It is proposed that natural antioxidants be used to prevent myocardial metabolic disorders in coronary patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
